  "plain": "The idea here is that the 1947 Roswell crash, the reported fall of an unknown object near Roswell, New Mexico, marks a turning point: before it, strange visitors show up as the beings of folklore, and after it, they show up as aliens. Michels says this is the theory he likes best, and he credits it to the UFO researcher Jacques Vallée and the religion scholar Diana Pasulka, calling 1947 and Roswell \"this dividing line.\" If it holds, the same phenomenon would simply have changed the face it shows people."
